# T0140 — MFA backup / recovery codes

**Task:** T0140 (id 153) · Parent: T0111 · Project: TaskMesh (4)  
**Branch (on approval):** `T0140-mfa-backup-codes`  
**State at plan:** Ready  

## Goal

Users with MFA enrolled can generate one-time backup/recovery codes to regain access if they lose their authenticator, without needing an Admin MFA clear in every case. Codes are single-use, stored hashed, shown plaintext once, and accepted on the MFA challenge step in place of TOTP.

## Interview decisions (locked)

| # | Topic | Decision |
|---|--------|----------|
| 1 | When codes are issued | After successful enroll confirm: **required** one-time reveal (cannot finish enroll without acknowledging). Profile can **regenerate** later with confirm. |
| 2 | Set size / format | **10** codes, `XXXX-XXXX` (uppercase alphanumeric, no ambiguous `0/O/1/I`), hashed at rest (SHA-256). |
| 3 | Login UX | Same challenge step: **“Use a backup code”** toggles input; shares existing attempt limit (5). |
| 4 | Regenerate | Requires current **TOTP** (not a recovery code). Invalidates entire previous set. Confirm dialog first. |
| 5 | Exhausted codes | Status shows **0 remaining**; login rejects; regenerate from Profile with TOTP (or Admin Clear MFA). |
| 6 | Admin | Show **has recovery codes** + remaining count (never plaintext). Clear MFA wipes recovery codes. |
| 7 | Enforced users | May regenerate while enrolled; still cannot self-disable MFA. |

## Out of scope

- Trusted device changes (T0141 already shipped)
- SMS / email / WebAuthn recovery
- Changing `dueDate` via worktask bookkeeping

## Technical approach

### Schema (new Drizzle migration → MINOR bump on finish-up)

- New table `mfa_recovery_codes`:
  - `id` serial PK
  - `user_id` FK → users (cascade)
  - `code_hash` text not null (SHA-256 hex of normalized code)
  - `used_at` timestamptz nullable
  - `created_at` timestamptz not null default now()
  - Unique on `(user_id, code_hash)` optional; index on `user_id`
- On disable / Admin clear MFA: delete all rows for that user

Update `docs/database/platform.md`; `docs:sync-schema` on finish-up.

### Server

- Generate 10 codes (`XXXX-XXXX` from alphabet without 0/O/1/I); normalize (strip dashes/spaces, uppercase) before hash/compare
- `confirmMfaEnrollment`: after TOTP OK, generate set, return plaintext codes once with status
- `POST /me/mfa/recovery-codes/regenerate` — body `{ code: TOTP }` → wipe old, mint new, return plaintext once
- `GET /me/mfa` status: add `recoveryCodesRemaining`, `hasRecoveryCodes`
- `verifyMfaChallenge`: if code looks like recovery (not 6-digit TOTP) or client sends `method: "recovery"`, verify hash match unused code → mark `used_at`, consume challenge; else existing TOTP path
- Rate limit: same challenge `failedAttempts` / max 5
- Admin user payload: `mfaRecoveryCodesRemaining` (or boolean + count)

### Client

- Enroll confirm success → mandatory backup-codes reveal card (copy all / acknowledge Done)
- Profile: remaining count + Regenerate (confirm + TOTP)
- Login MFA step: toggle “Use a backup code”
- Admin users: show recovery-code status when MFA enrolled

